WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.234
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:04.067
If you love seeing
new inventions

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:05.501
and you love brilliant kids,

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.567
then you're really going to
love this.

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.200
It is time for "Fallonventions."

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:12.100
Welcome to Fallonventions,

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.200
Jimmy Fallon's
night of invention.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:20.734
-Now, I love inventions
and I'm okay with kids.

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:24.367
So we found some of the best
and brightest kids out there,

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:25.534
and I think you're
going to be amazed

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:26.567
at what they came up with.

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:28.167
So, let's meet
our first inventor.

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:29.634
[ Drumroll
Come on over, Bekah.

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:30.801
Hey.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:33.868
♪♪

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:36.267
Thank you. Nice to see you.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:38.367
Yeah.
You want to give me those, too?

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:40.267
Bekah, how old are you?

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:42.601
-I'm 9 and I'm from
Boston, Massachusetts.

00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:45.901
-Hey!
From Boston, Massachusetts.

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.834
I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:49.934
Is this your invention?
What is your invention?

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:51.701
-This is my invention,
and I call it

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:53.133
The Mighty Suction Holders.

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.767
-The Mighty Suction Holders.

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:57.000
Okay. And, now, what does it do?

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.067
-My younger brother
used to stand up on the chairs

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:03.100
and tip the chairs so that
he would fall over and get hurt.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.667
And in church,
we're learning that God wants us

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:07.334
to use our talents
to help other people,

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:09.934
so I made this invention
to help younger kids

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:11.734
from falling over
in their chairs.

00:01:11.734 --> 00:01:13.067
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:15.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:17.567
-We have a chair right here,

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:20.133
so we can see how
this invention works.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:22.567
Can I help you with this?
So, this is the chair here.

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:24.701
So, your brother would stand
on this and fall over.

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:26.868
-Yes.
-Yeah, we can't have that.

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:28.367
Alright, come on.
Let's fix this.

00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:29.767
Alright, here we go.

00:01:29.767 --> 00:01:33.601
Roots, can I get some
suction-cup-leg music?

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:35.000
♪♪

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.067
Is there a theme for -- Alright.

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:38.367
Yeah, am I doing it right?
-Yeah.

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:41.267
-Bekah, thank you.
That's correct.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:46.033
That's it, right? Good?
Does that feel good?

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:48.434
Alright, here we go.
Let me try it out.

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:52.767
[ Drumroll ]

00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:54.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:04.200
That's what I'm talking about.
That is a great invention.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.934
Thank you so much.
That is a really good invention.

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:08.834
Oh, Bekah, do you want to see
an invention I made?

00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:10.667
-Yes.
-Okay, cool.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.200
I have an invention.
This is cool.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.501
I think you're
going to like this.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:18.400
Alright, this is called --
This is --

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.667
You ever have a conversation
with your buddy at school

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:24.968
and you wish
you had more privacy?

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:26.634
Yeah?

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:28.934
Well, now you can totally get
all the privacy you want.

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:31.534
They're called
Private Chat Helmets, okay?

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:33.467
And they let you have
a totally private conversation

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:35.000
wherever you are, right?

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.501
Check this out.

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:40.400
It's very easy to put on.
Do you want to try it on?

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:52.167
Hey, Bekah.

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:53.734
-Yes?

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:55.701
-You're from Boston, right?

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:56.934
-Yes.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:03:00.133
-What's your go-to order
at Dunkin'?

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:04.200
-My parents would prefer
Starbucks.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.200
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:20.934
-Let's meet our
next inventor, Liana.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.000
Liana, come on over.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:03:27.567 --> 00:03:29.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:31.601
Sorry.

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:33.334
[ Grunts ]

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:35.033
Gosh. Man, oh, man.

00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:38.968
I don't know what her brother
is doing on these chairs.

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:40.300
Liana.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.901
-Hi.
-Hi. Welcome.

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:45.200
Thank you for being here.
Where are you from?

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.300
-Fairfield, Connecticut.
-Fairfield, Connecticut.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:50.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
What is your invention?

00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:52.200
-The Zero Mess Tray.
-What is it called?

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.634
-The Zero Mess Tray.
-The Zero Mess Tray.

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.834
Oh, maybe I'll bring that
chair back in, actually.

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:58.534
Alright, perfect.
The Zero Mess Tray.

00:03:58.534 --> 00:04:01.801
And can I try it on?
I think I know how this goes.

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:05.667
-Zero-mess, so, I'm --
Is it for eating or just for --

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:07.968
-It's to prevent messes
on the go.

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:09.234
-Yeah, so you're on the go.

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:11.000
You don't know when
it might get messy.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.734
-Yeah.
-You throw this on.

00:04:12.734 --> 00:04:14.501
And this rolls in.
This all fits in together?

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:15.567
-Mm-hmm.
-Okay, cool.

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:17.868
What can I have here
that's messy?

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:20.601
Yeah. Thank you so much.

00:04:20.601 --> 00:04:22.434
So, I eat this mess.

00:04:22.434 --> 00:04:24.133
Someone gives me a taco,
I'm like, "Dude, let's go.

00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:25.701
What's up?"

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:27.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:28.934
Right?

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:31.634
-Yeah.
-Go like this.

00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:33.501
Push it in there?
-Uh-huh.

00:04:33.501 --> 00:04:34.567
-You take it off?
-Take it off.

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.567
-Yeah, that's what
I'm talking about.

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:37.901
There's your mess, right there.
Look at this.

00:04:37.901 --> 00:04:40.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.467
This is good.

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:45.901
Liana, let me show you
an invention I had here.

00:04:45.901 --> 00:04:47.868
This is perfect for
The Zero Mess Tray.

00:04:47.868 --> 00:04:50.167
Oh -- Oh, yeah,
thank you so much.

00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:51.467
Check this out, right?

00:04:51.467 --> 00:04:52.968
So, you're just
hanging out, right?

00:04:52.968 --> 00:04:56.067
Gosh. Oh, here you go.

00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:59.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:03.067
That's how I put my ties on --
all Velcro.

00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:04.300
So, I'm hanging out, right?

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:05.667
We're hanging out.
We're having a good time, right?

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:07.701
I'm eating tacos.
You're hanging out.

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:10.200
I go, "Yeah,
you got any hot sauce?"

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.868
-Uh, no.
-Yeah, you don't. Yeah.

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:13.501
No problem. I've got it handled.

00:05:13.501 --> 00:05:15.501
You take normal -- It looks
normal, this tie, right?

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:17.200
-Mm-hmm.
-No.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.567
Check out this.

00:05:18.567 --> 00:05:21.701
You flip this switch here.

00:05:21.701 --> 00:05:24.067
Look at that.

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:27.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.734
Put that there.
you close this nozzle here,

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:32.534
and then you have
all the hot sauce you want.

00:05:32.534 --> 00:05:34.434
And make all the mess.
You like it?

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:35.801
-Yeah, I love it.
-Hot.

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:38.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:39.200
Alright, thank you
for coming on, Liana.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:41.467
I appreciate it.

00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:44.234
This is fantastic.
And not a mess on me.

00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:45.667
This is amazing. Thank you.
Be careful.

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:47.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:52.067
Let's meet our last inventor.
Come on over, Remi.

00:05:52.067 --> 00:05:53.367
Come on over here.

00:05:53.367 --> 00:05:55.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:05:58.400 --> 00:05:59.534
-Remi, welcome to the show.

00:05:59.534 --> 00:06:01.000
How old are you
and where are you from?

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:04.167
-I'm 10 years old and I'm from
Torrance, California.

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:07.434
-Hey, come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:08.567
I'm so happy. 10 years --

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.534
And what is
your invention here, Remi?

00:06:10.534 --> 00:06:12.734
-Well, I invented Rubbie Blinds.

00:06:12.734 --> 00:06:15.033
-Rubbie -- What is it?
-Rubbie Blinds.

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:16.400
-Rubbie Blinds.
-Yes.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.634
-Okay, what is Rubbie Blinds?

00:06:18.634 --> 00:06:23.567
-well, so, I have a cat,
and it always, like,

00:06:23.567 --> 00:06:24.734
breaks our blinds.

00:06:24.734 --> 00:06:28.534
So, the way it works is, like --

00:06:28.534 --> 00:06:30.601
So, let's say, like,
the cat's inside,

00:06:30.601 --> 00:06:34.133
and it wants to come out.

00:06:34.133 --> 00:06:36.868
If it bends the blinds,
then comes out --

00:06:36.868 --> 00:06:38.200
-So, you have no windows
in the glass?

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:40.100
You just --
-Yeah, exactly.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:43.100
-Yeah. You like fresh air
in the house,

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.701
but you also want your privacy.

00:06:44.701 --> 00:06:47.868
So you leave the windows open,
you get Rubbie Blinds.

00:06:47.868 --> 00:06:49.133
Don't look in here.

00:06:49.133 --> 00:06:51.701
And then your cat sneaks
in and out of that one up there?

00:06:51.701 --> 00:06:53.133
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:06:53.133 --> 00:06:55.367
-And then you can just, like,
fix it by bending them back.

00:06:55.367 --> 00:06:57.467
-What's the cat's name?

00:06:57.467 --> 00:06:59.767
-My cat or this cat?

00:06:59.767 --> 00:07:02.567
-Hmm. That's a good question.

00:07:02.567 --> 00:07:04.434
I'm going to say this cat.

00:07:04.434 --> 00:07:06.868
-This is Midnight Jr.
-Oh!

00:07:06.868 --> 00:07:08.834
And Midnight Jr. comes
in through this thing, right?

00:07:08.834 --> 00:07:10.701
And he gets stuck in
the blinds, like that.

00:07:10.701 --> 00:07:12.000
And you go, "No, Midnight Jr."

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:16.567
And he's a bad -- "Midnight Jr.,
no coming into the house.

00:07:16.567 --> 00:07:18.200
You have to stay out tonight."

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.234
And he goes out.

00:07:19.234 --> 00:07:21.334
And this is based on
your real cat?

00:07:21.334 --> 00:07:22.601
-Yeah.
-What's your real cat's name?

00:07:22.601 --> 00:07:24.133
-Midnight.
-There you go.

00:07:24.133 --> 00:07:25.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:25.968 --> 00:07:27.467
Unbelievable.

00:07:29.133 --> 00:07:31.801
That's a great --
I like Rubbie Blinds.

00:07:31.801 --> 00:07:33.968
Guys, can we get all
the kid inventors out here?

00:07:33.968 --> 00:07:35.801
This is fantastic.

00:07:35.801 --> 00:07:38.367
Here's Midnight Jr.

00:07:38.367 --> 00:07:39.701
We here at "The Tonight Show"

00:07:39.701 --> 00:07:42.634
love supporting
smart, talented kids like you.

00:07:42.634 --> 00:07:45.067
We want to help you keep
exploring and creating

00:07:45.067 --> 00:07:47.400
and changing the world,
so we're giving each of you

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.334
$5,000 to help further
your education.

00:07:49.334 --> 00:07:54.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
Giant check.

00:07:54.801 --> 00:07:56.200
Here, Rebekah, that's a giant --

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.033
-Thank you.
-There you go.

00:08:00.434 --> 00:08:02.400
Liana, that's for you.
-Thank you.

00:08:04.133 --> 00:08:07.300
Here you go, Remi.
That's for you and Midnight Jr.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:08.367
That's what I'm talking about.

00:08:08.367 --> 00:08:10.934
Thanks to Bekah, Liana,
and Remi.

00:08:10.934 --> 00:08:12.200
Stick around.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:14.400
We'll be right with
Kerry Washington, everybody.

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:15.467
That was great!

